by nicolas-grekas at 2026-07-29T14:09:52Z

Thanks Ousama. I rebased on 8.2, squashed to one commit and made a few changes before merging:

* Dropped `BinaryContentEncoder`. The `Content-Transfer-Encoding` header comes from `TextPart::$encoding`, not from the encoder, and `getName()` is only used by `addEncoder()` as a registry key, so `binary` can map to `EightBitContentEncoder` directly. Both encoders returned the body untouched, so the bytes on the wire are the same and we avoid a new public class.
* `addEncoder()` now checks its own list of names instead of `DEFAULT_ENCODERS`. Adding `binary` to that constant would have made `addEncoder()` reject a custom `binary` encoder, which is the workaround described in #60301, so upgrading would have broken the people this feature is for.
* Moved the CHANGELOG entry to the `8.2` section. The `8.1` section it created does not exist in this file.

Mime and Mailer suites are green.
